FAQ = [
 ("How long is a short bed truck?",
  "It depends on the truck, because short is a name, not a size. On the 2019–2026 Chevy Silverado 1500 and GMC Sierra 1500 the short bed is 69.9 in. Ford's shortest F-150 bed is the 5.5 ft, which measures 67.1 in, and the Ram 1500's 5'7\" bed is 67.4 in. On midsize trucks the short bed is about 5 ft: 60.5 in on the 2016–2023 Toyota Tacoma, 60 in on the 2024–2026 Tacoma and 59.6 in on the 2024–2026 Ford Ranger. The Ford Maverick's only bed is 54.4 in. Always shop by the inch figure for your truck and generation."),
 ("How do I measure my truck bed for a tonneau cover?",
  "Close the tailgate and measure inside the bed, along the top of the bed rail, from the front bulkhead to the inside edge of the tailgate. RealTruck's guide says to measure at the top of the bed rails, not the floor. Write the number down in inches, then match it to the chart on this page. Don't round it yourself and don't convert it to feet before you shop. A cover is sold by the maker's part number for one bed, and the inch figure in the listing title is what tells you which bed that part is for."),
 ("Why is my 5.5 ft bed 67 inches and not 66?",
  "Because the foot figure is a name. RealTruck's measuring guide says manufacturers typically round bed sizes to the nearest half-foot for marketing. Ford calls the F-150's shortest bed 5.5 ft, which would be 66 in, but it measures 67.1 in at the rail. That is why cover retailers print 5'7\" on the same bed. The same thing happens on other trucks: the Tundra's 5.5 ft bed is listed at 66.7 in, and the F-150's 8 ft bed is 97.6 in, which retailers label 8'2\". The inches are the fact, and the feet are the label."),
 ("Is a 5'7\" bed the same on every truck?",
  "No. Three trucks in the site's guides have a bed that retailers label 5'7\": the F-150 at 67.1 in, the Ram 1500 at 67.4 in and the 2022–2026 Tundra at 66.7 in. The lengths are close, but the beds have different rails, tailgates and options, so the covers carry different part numbers. BAK's MX4, for example, is 448339 for the 2021+ F-150 and 448440 for the 2022+ Tundra. A matching label tells you nothing about fit. The listing has to name your make, model and model years."),
 ("Does a crew cab always have the short bed?",
  "No, and that is the most common ordering mistake. On the F-150, a SuperCrew can have the 5.5 ft or the 6.5 ft bed. A Silverado Crew Cab can have the short or the standard bed. A Tundra CrewMax comes with the 5.5 ft or 6.5 ft bed, and a Tacoma Double Cab usually has the 5 ft bed but could be ordered with the 6 ft. The reverse traps exist too: every 2017–2020 F-150 Raptor has the 5.5 ft bed, including the SuperCab. The cab narrows the options. Only a tape measure settles it."),
 ("What bed lengths does the Ford F-150 come with?",
  "Three, and they are the same on the 2015–2020 and 2021–2026 trucks: 5.5 ft (67.1 in), 6.5 ft (78.9 in) and 8 ft (97.6 in), measured inside at the rail. Retailers label them 5'7\", 6'7\" and 8' or 8'2\". On the current truck the 5.5 ft bed is SuperCrew only and is the only bed on the Raptor and Lightning. The 6.5 ft bed comes on SuperCrew, SuperCab and Regular Cab. The 8 ft bed comes on the Regular Cab, and on the SuperCab through 2023. Covers are still split by generation, so buy the part listed for your model year."),
 ("What bed lengths do the Silverado 1500 and Sierra 1500 come with?",
  "The 2019–2026 trucks share three beds: short at 69.9 in, standard at 79.4 in and long at 98.2 in, measured at the floor. The short bed comes only on the Crew Cab, the standard bed on Double Cab and Crew Cab, and the long bed on the Regular Cab. Cover makers label the short bed 5'8\" or 5'10\", the standard 6'6\" or 6'7\" and the long 8' or 8'2\". Watch for the 2019 Silverado LD and 2019 Sierra Limited. They are the older body with a bed of about 69 in and take 2014–2018 parts."),
 ("What are the Toyota Tacoma's bed lengths?",
  "Two per generation, and the generations are not interchangeable. The 2016–2023 Tacoma has a 5 ft bed that retailers list at 60.5 in (5'1\") and a 6 ft bed at 73.7 in (6'2\"). The 2024–2026 Tacoma has a 5 ft bed listed at 60 in and a 6 ft bed that makers print as anything from 72 to 74 in. The Access Cab and the newer XtraCab come only with the 6 ft bed. Double Cabs have either. Makers sell separate parts for each generation, such as BAKFlip MX4 448426 for 2016–2023 and 448446 for 2024 and later."),
 ("Will a cover from the previous generation fit if the bed length is the same?",
  "Usually not, and the makers' part numbers show it. The F-150 kept its 67.1 and 78.9 in beds from 2015 to 2026, yet BAK lists the MX4 as 448329 for 2015–2020 and 448339 for 2021 and later. The 2022 Tundra kept the old bed names with a new composite bed and new parts. There are exceptions: TruXedo lists its Lo Pro 597701 for 2015–2026 F-150s. The safe rule is to buy the part number the maker lists for your model year, and to check the label on any used cover before you pay."),
 ("Do RamBox, CarbonPro or MultiPro change the bed length?",
  "No. They change the part number. A Ram 1500 with RamBox bins still has the 67.4 in bed, but it needs RamBox-specific covers and racks. A Sierra with the CarbonPro composite bed is still the 69.9 in short bed, but the big makers sell separate CarbonPro parts and list their standard covers as not for it. MultiPro and Multi-Flex tailgates don't change length or, on the covers in the site's guides, fit. They change how you use the inner gate with the cover closed. Measure for the length, then check the bed sides and tailgate for the option."),
 ("Do bed racks depend on bed length too?",
  "Yes. Racks are sized to the bed, and many mount to stake pockets or factory rail systems, so a short-bed rack won't reach the mounting points on a long bed. Putco, for example, lists separate versions of its rack for the Silverado's 5'8\" and 6'6\" beds. Factory hardware matters as much as length: the site's data notes that most Tacoma racks clamp to the factory deck rails, that RamBox trucks need RamBox-specific racks, and that the Gladiator's optional Trail Rail system changes rack fit. If you plan to run a rack with a tonneau cover, check both listings for compatibility."),
]

